workedExamples.solution_text:
There are four directed paths.

Path $A$–$D$–$F$:
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}7+4+3\\&=14\text{ hours}\end{aligned}$

Path $A$–$E$–$F$:
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}7+6+3\\&=16\text{ hours}\end{aligned}$

Path $B$–$C$–$D$–$F$:
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}4+3+4+3\\&=14\text{ hours}\end{aligned}$

Path $B$–$C$–$E$–$F$:
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}4+3+6+3\\&=16\text{ hours}\end{aligned}$

Both $A$–$E$–$F$ and $B$–$C$–$E$–$F$ have the greatest length. They are the two critical paths, and the minimum completion time is $16$ hours.

